<!-- The Audiences area of IronStone Marketing (design-marketing §4, §1.2; impl-marketing P3): Lists (the organizations' lists, New
    list), Consent (Comms' Consent screens mounted by location, with Marketing's organizations and MARKETING_CONSENT_EDIT: their
    services answer a Marketing consent editor for the lists and scoped consents of their organizations, F50) and Suppressions
    (Comms' shared screen, Marketing's mount, F16), in the menu; ListDetail and MemberDetail hidden. For the audience managers and the
    administrator (BOSS_MKT_AUDIENCES denies the root user group; the root's menu shows it to a holder of MARKETING_AUDIENCE_VIEW);
    every read and write is Mantle's guarded audience, consent or suppression service. AudienceImport and AudienceMerge (P4) are
    hidden, opened from Lists and ListDetail. Comms' Consent keeps its own subscreen names (Consent and Consent/Contact), so its
    relative links hold.
    P5: Segments (index 2) and SegmentDetail (hidden), the audience managers'; AudiencePreview (index 6), which the authors and
    dispatchers also open past the area's deny (BOSS_MKT_AUDIENCE_PREVIEW: an ALWAYS on this screen that does not pass to its other
    subscreens, and an inheritable one on AudiencePreview), its rows masked for them by Mantle's preview#Audience. -->
<screen xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://moqui.org/xsd/mr-xml-screen.xsd"
        default-menu-title="Audiences" default-menu-index="3" menu-image="sym_o_groups" menu-image-type="icon">
    <subscreens default-item="Lists" always-use-full-path="true">
        <subscreens-item name="Consent" location="component://mr-boss/screen/Comms/Consent.xml" menu-index="3"/>
        <subscreens-item name="Suppressions" location="component://mr-boss/screen/Shared/Suppressions.xml" menu-index="4"/>
    </subscreens>
    <widgets>
        <subscreens-panel id="MarketingAudiencesPanel" type="tab"/>
    </widgets>
</screen>
